# Engineering rigor (all work)

Applies to every task — UI, backend, RLS, copy, and infra — not only frontend files.

## Verify, don’t guess

- Check the actual source of truth before acting (RLS policies in migrations / live `pg_policies`, route existence under `app/`, real column names, existing helpers).
- Prefer reading the relevant file/section over assuming from memory or product copy.
- If production state may differ from repo migrations, say so explicitly.

## Reuse before inventing

- Search for existing utilities, hooks, components, and API routes first.
- Extend shared patterns (`lib/`, `hooks/`, `components/`) instead of duplicating near-copies.
- Match local naming, error handling, and style of the surrounding code.

## Flag inconsistencies

- Surface mismatches you notice (copy vs behavior, badge vs RLS, dead links, dual sources of truth) even when not asked to fix them.
- For UI-touching work, also apply `.cursor/rules/margo-ui-design-system.mdc` and `MARGO_BRAND.md` Sections 14–15 — flag requests that would violate those standards before building.

## Minimal, surgical changes

- Targeted diffs only; don’t restructure files to fix one issue.
- No drive-by refactors or unrequested docs.
